# Service Architecture & Patterns

## 🏗️ Service Categories

### Core System Services
Business logic and system management services:

#### Authentication & Security
- **[AuthService](mdc:src/app/services/auth.service.ts)**: User authentication and JWT token management
- **[UserService](mdc:src/app/services/user.service.ts)**: User account operations and profile management

#### Configuration & Certificate
- **[ConfigurationService](mdc:src/app/services/configuration.service.ts)**: System configuration management
- **[CertificateService](mdc:src/app/services/certificate.service.ts)**: SSL certificate management

#### Data & Analytics
- **[StatisticsService](mdc:src/app/services/statistics.service.ts)**: System metrics and analytics
- **[AssetsService](mdc:src/app/services/assets.service.ts)**: IoT asset data management

### Infrastructure Services
Application infrastructure and utility services:

#### Communication & Monitoring
- **[PingService](mdc:src/app/services/ping.service.ts)**: System health monitoring and connectivity checks
- **[SharedService](mdc:src/app/services/shared.service.ts)**: Global state management and component communication
- **[AlertService](mdc:src/app/services/alert.service.ts)**: User notifications and alert management

#### Logging & Debugging
- **[SystemLogService](mdc:src/app/services/system-log.service.ts)**: System log retrieval and filtering
- **[PackagesLogService](mdc:src/app/services/packages-log.service.ts)**: Package installation and update logs
- **[AuditService](mdc:src/app/services/audit.service.ts)**: System audit trail and activity logging

## 🎯 Service Implementation Patterns

### Standard Service Structure
```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
import { BehaviorSubject, Observable } from 'rxjs';
import { catchError, map, tap } from 'rxjs/operators';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root' // or feature module level
})
export class ServiceName {
  // 1. Private API base URL
  private readonly apiUrl = environment.BASE_URL;
  
  // 2. State management with BehaviorSubjects
  private dataSubject = new BehaviorSubject<DataType[]>([]);
  private loadingSubject = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);
  
  // 3. Public observables
  public data$ = this.dataSubject.asObservable();
  public loading$ = this.loadingSubject.asObservable();
  
  // 4. Constructor with dependency injection
  constructor(
    private http: HttpClient,
    private alertService: AlertService
  ) {}
  
  // 5. CRUD operations
  public getData(): Observable<DataType[]> {
    this.loadingSubject.next(true);
    return this.http.get<DataType[]>(`${this.apiUrl}/data`)
      .pipe(
        tap(data => {
          this.dataSubject.next(data);
          this.loadingSubject.next(false);
        }),
        catchError(error => this.handleError(error))
      );
  }
  
  public createItem(item: DataType): Observable<DataType> {
    return this.http.post<DataType>(`${this.apiUrl}/data`, item)
      .pipe(
        tap(newItem => {
          const currentData = this.dataSubject.getValue();
          this.dataSubject.next([...currentData, newItem]);
        }),
        catchError(error => this.handleError(error))
      );
  }
  
  // 6. Error handling
  private handleError(error: any): Observable<never> {
    console.error('Service error:', error);
    this.alertService.error(error.message || 'An error occurred');
    this.loadingSubject.next(false);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

### Reactive State Management Pattern
Services use BehaviorSubjects for state management:

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class StateService {
  // Private state
  private userStateSubject = new BehaviorSubject<UserState>({
    loggedIn: false,
    user: null
  });
  
  private connectionInfoSubject = new BehaviorSubject<ConnectionInfo>(null);
  
  // Public observables
  public userState$ = this.userStateSubject.asObservable();
  public connectionInfo$ = this.connectionInfoSubject.asObservable();
  
  // State update methods
  public updateUserState(state: UserState): void {
    this.userStateSubject.next(state);
  }
  
  public updateConnectionInfo(info: ConnectionInfo): void {
    this.connectionInfoSubject.next(info);
  }
  
  // State getters
  public getCurrentUserState(): UserState {
    return this.userStateSubject.getValue();
  }
}
```

## 🔄 Shared Service Pattern

The [SharedService](mdc:src/app/services/shared.service.ts) manages global application state:

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class SharedService {
  // Authentication state
  public isUserLoggedIn: BehaviorSubject<any> = new BehaviorSubject<any>(false);
  public isAdmin: BehaviorSubject<boolean> = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);
  
  // UI state
  public theme: BehaviorSubject<string> = new BehaviorSubject<string>('light');
  public isSidebarCollapsed: BehaviorSubject<boolean> = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(true);
  public loginScreenSubject: BehaviorSubject<boolean> = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);
  
  // System state
  public connectionInfo: BehaviorSubject<any> = new BehaviorSubject<any>(false);
  public viewport: BehaviorSubject<any> = new BehaviorSubject<any>(false);
  
  // Utility methods
  public checkAuth(): boolean {
    const auth = !JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('LOGIN_SKIPPED'));
    const admin = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('isAdmin'));
    return auth ? admin : true;
  }
}
```

## 📡 HTTP Service Patterns

### API Service Base Class
Create a base class for common HTTP operations:

```typescript
export abstract class BaseApiService {
  protected abstract apiUrl: string;
  
  constructor(protected http: HttpClient) {}
  
  protected get<T>(endpoint: string): Observable<T> {
    return this.http.get<T>(`${this.apiUrl}${endpoint}`)
      .pipe(catchError(this.handleError));
  }
  
  protected post<T>(endpoint: string, data: any): Observable<T> {
    return this.http.post<T>(`${this.apiUrl}${endpoint}`, data)
      .pipe(catchError(this.handleError));
  }
  
  protected put<T>(endpoint: string, data: any): Observable<T> {
    return this.http.put<T>(`${this.apiUrl}${endpoint}`, data)
      .pipe(catchError(this.handleError));
  }
  
  protected delete<T>(endpoint: string): Observable<T> {
    return this.http.delete<T>(`${this.apiUrl}${endpoint}`)
      .pipe(catchError(this.handleError));
  }
  
  protected handleError(error: HttpErrorResponse): Observable<never> {
    console.error('API Error:', error);
    // Handle specific error codes
    if (error.status === 401) {
      // Handle unauthorized
    }
    throw error;
  }
}
```

### Specialized Service Implementation
```typescript
@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class DataService extends BaseApiService {
  protected apiUrl = `${environment.BASE_URL}/api/data`;
  
  constructor(
    http: HttpClient,
    private alertService: AlertService
  ) {
    super(http);
  }
  
  public getItems(): Observable<Item[]> {
    return this.get<Item[]>('/items')
      .pipe(
        tap(items => console.log('Retrieved items:', items.length))
      );
  }
  
  public createItem(item: CreateItemRequest): Observable<Item> {
    return this.post<Item>('/items', item)
      .pipe(
        tap(newItem => this.alertService.success('Item created successfully'))
      );
  }
}
```

## 🔧 Service Configuration & Providers

### Service Provider Configuration
```typescript
// In app.module.ts
providers: [
  {
    provide: 'ALERT_SERVICE',
    useExisting: AlertService,
  },
  {
    provide: 'SHARED_SERVICE',
    useExisting: SharedService
  },
  {
    provide: HTTP_INTERCEPTORS,
    useClass: HttpsRequestInterceptor,
    multi: true,
  }
]
```

### Factory Providers
Use factory functions for complex service initialization:

```typescript
export function pingServiceFactory(
  ping: PingService, 
  sharedService: SharedService, 
  router: Router
): Function {
  return () => ping.pingService()
    .then((data) => {
      sessionStorage.setItem('LOGIN_SKIPPED', JSON.stringify(data['authenticationOptional']));
      // Handle authentication flow
    })
    .catch(error => {
      // Handle connection errors
    });
}

// In providers array
{
  provide: APP_INITIALIZER,
  useFactory: pingServiceFactory,
  deps: [PingService, SharedService, Router],
  multi: true
}
```

## 🎯 Performance & Best Practices

### Memory Management
- Properly unsubscribe from observables
- Use takeUntil pattern in services when needed
- Clear BehaviorSubject references on service destruction

### Caching Strategies
- Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- Consider using HTTP interceptors for response caching

### Error Handling
- Implement consistent error handling across all services
- Use centralized error logging
- Provide meaningful error messages to users